 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Time changes",
   "texto": [
    "By telling something from a later moment, we often move time: **Estou cansado** → **Disse que estava cansado** (he said he was tired). If the information is still in place, the present can also be maintained: **Disse que está cansado** (he said he is tired)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The future goes to parole",
   "texto": [
    "**Virei amanhã** (I will come tomorrow) → **Disse que viria no dia seguinte** (said I would come the next day), if we report from the day after. Time expressions also depend on the moment we count: **amanhã** can be maintained if it is still tomorrow."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "That",
   "texto": [
    "It binds to **que**: **disse que** (said it). People change as in Spanish: **Estou cansado** → **Ela disse que estava cansada**."
   ]
  },
